*** Add File:ops/runbooks/Operator_Autonomy_Playbook.md
+# Operator Playbook: From scaffold to production-grade autonomous flows
+
+This runbook describes the concrete human steps and approvals required to safely enable automated retrain/promote flows and RL-driven policy actions.
+
+1) Pre-deployment checks
+ - Ensure KMS keys exist and cosign signing is functional; cosign must sign artifacts produced by CI.
+ - Ensure ValidatingWebhookConfiguration for cosign is in place for production namespaces.
+ - Confirm S3 buckets with Object Lock enabled for evidence and artifacts used for compliance (legal signoff).
+
+2) Argo workflow readiness
+ - Ensure argo-workflow-sa has limited RBAC scoped to ml-pipelines namespace.
+ - Ensure PV/PVC used by workflows are backed up and have sufficient capacity.
+ - Validate finetune container images (reproducible builds) and that metadata service is reachable.
+
+3) Canary strategy
+ - Shadow for minimum 7 days or 100k inference samples.
+ - Canary 1% → 5% → 10% with 24–72h observation windows; require SME signoff between steps.
+
+4) Enabling RL actions
+ - RL agent outputs must produce a manual-approval request before any cluster modification.
+ - Only after human approval in the manual-approval service may the operator apply changes recommended by RL agent.
+
+5) Incident & rollback
+ - If canary or spec acceptance metrics breach thresholds, run argo rollback template and create an incident ticket.
+ - Follow SLO runbook to scale rater capacity and initiate urgent retrain if verifier regression observed.
+
